<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n37065" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐξεικ-άζω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>make like, adapt,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αὑτὸν ταῖς τῶν φιλούντων ὑπουργίαις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					X.
					<u>Hier.</u>
					1.38
				</span></i>
			:—
				Pass.
			, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐξείκαστό τινι</span>
			<i>was like</i> it, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Cyr.</u>
				1.6.39
			</span></i>: mostly in pf.
			part., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐδὲν
			ἐξῃκασμένα</span> not <i>mere semblances,</i> but the things
			themselves, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Ag.</u>
				1244
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κεραυνὸν οὐδὲν ἐξῃκασμένον . .
					θάλπεσιν τοῖς ἡλίου</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Th.</u>
					445
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στέρνα τ᾽ ἐξῃκασμένα</span>”
				<i>portrayed,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Ph.</u>
					162
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐ γάρ ἐστιν
			ἐξῃκασμένος</span> he is not <i>represented by a
				portrait-mask,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Eq.</u>
				230
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
